1
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,840
Aaaaaaah

2
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:46,580
Aaaaaaah

3
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:03,620
Anyone without a job, come see me.
I don't have one either, but I'm worried.

4
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:04,420
Me

5
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,240
Me

6
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,740
The king of refusing lemons
without even trying them

7
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:54,360
What, you're still sleeping?
Hurry up and get up.

8
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,360
It's still early, isn't it?

9
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:01,640
What are you talking about?
Stop whining and get up quickly.

10
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:11,080
You're not just short-tempered,
you're impatient.

11
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,040
Kankichi

12
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,900
Good morning to me too.

13
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,840
Kankichi, look!

14
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,680
Isn't that a randoseru?

15
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:20,940
Because I start first grade next year.

16
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,920
Grandma bought it for me.

17
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:26,240
I see. It suits you really well.

18
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,040
Grandma's getting ahead of herself.

19
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:32,860
Off you go, miss. Take care!

20
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:34,120
Wait for me!

21
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,740
Isn't that way too early, no matter what?

22
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:44,120
I love the air of this quiet morning,
the kind you get used to.

23
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:47,400
My elementary school was close,
so I went a bit later than that.

24
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,420
But from middle school on,
I always left the house at this time.

25
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:55,480
So, I was always the first one to school.

26
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:59,220
My family also ran a tsukudani shop,
so we were up early, too.

27
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,520
I was always late, though.

28
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,780
Your home's the slow one. Hurry up already.

29
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:09,860
Normally it's the women who take longer,
putting on makeup and such.

30
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,740
Why are you so fast, Mati?

31
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:15,920
Well, it's just washing my face, brushing
my teeth, and eating breakfast, right?

32
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,480
It takes five minutes, tops.

33
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:22,220
That's too fast! Maria said her
morning shampoo takes an hour.

34
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:24,720
An hour? Shampoo's at night, isn't it?

35
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,300
You

36
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,720
The climb is something else.

37
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,640
Uh...

38
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:56,280
The morning train going down is empty and easy,
isn't it?

39
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:59,960
But I'm not fond of that long escalator.

40
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,100
It always feels like everyone's watching me.

41
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,680
Nobody even looks at an old geezer like me.

42
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:17,160
Kameari, Kameari.

43
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,340
Some lively early-risers over there, too.

44
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,900
Lemon's going to be a first-grader next year

45
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,160
A shiny new first-grader

46
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,700
The bus is here.

47
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:37,080
Well, I'm heading to the police box.

48
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,500
Yeah.

49
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:39,320
Right, Kankichi.

50
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,260
I made trout sushi for lunch.

51
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,500
I made some for you too, Kankichi.

52
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,000
Come eat it during your lunch break.

53
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,760
Yeah, see ya.

54
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,080
Chief Ohara, what's wrong?

55
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,900
Ryotsu, you...

56
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,820
He came all the way here
without even stopping in Shikoku.

57
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:09,520
But there's no need to be so surprised,
is there?

58
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:12,000
Is it going to snow today or something?

59
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:17,240
Apparently she came to work from
Matoi-chan's family home this morning.

60
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,420
Here's your tea.

61
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,440
Here you go, Chief, yours too.

62
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:22,100
Thank you.

63
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:26,200
Ryotsu, did you work part-time
at Matoi's house again?

64
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,480
Because it's before payday.

65
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,120
Well, it's less a part-time job than...

66
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:33,240
...more like we went
there to get a free meal.

67
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:36,240
So I came to work with Matoi-chan.

68
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:43,100
That's how it is. Taga came out early,
and that just makes the day longer.

69
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:51,380
Matoi is really a nuisance. He's always late and barely does any work,
so what's he talking about, you idiot?

70
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:55,740
Why are you getting so angry?
What? No, it's nothing.

71
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,920
Matoi-chan, is that sushi?

72
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,680
Yeah, trout sushi.

73
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,660
I made it at home this morning.

74
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:11,720
That looks delicious. Can I have one?

75
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:12,960
Go ahead.

76
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:17,340
Wow, it's delicious!

77
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:19,060
Senior Komachi, have one too.

78
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:22,020
Sorry, I don't like fish cured in vinegar.

79
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:23,758
But it's so good,

80
00:06:23,808 --> 00:06:26,760
Komachi,
you really are picky about your food.

81
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:30,940
Besides, I can't stand hijiki either.
Does anyone want it?

82
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,220
I got these.

83
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:34,793
Kankichi Ryotsu,

84
00:06:34,843 --> 00:06:38,660
Who said I was giving it to you?

85
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,600
Well, I already ate it.

86
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:44,360
Honestly, you really are a cockroach.

87
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:47,980
Or rather, it's your fault for being picky.

88
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:49,600
Shut up.

89
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:52,920
You've got one or two things
you don't like too, right?

90
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:57,120
In my case, there are only two categories:
like and love.

91
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,680
A cockroach I'm an idiot for asking.

92
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,280
Anyway, I'm a cockroach.

93
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:07,880
Speaking of likes and dislikes,
I've got a bit of a problem with lemons.

94
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,520
Lemons

95
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:41,000
Itamachi

96
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:42,560
Yes.

97
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:44,740
Its flavor lacks direction, doesn't it.

98
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:47,700
Meimon Kikka

99
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,760
Wakaiseki

100
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,380
True, it's a popular place right now.

101
00:07:57,280 --> 00:08:00,020
Maybe it's impossible
not to be conscious of it.

102
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,200
But it's not necessary.

103
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,140
Chokanda has a flavor all its own.

104
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:08,160
It may look plain, though.

105
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:10,820
It tastes good.

106
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:12,820
Have some confidence.

107
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:15,340
Here you go, Lady Lemon.

108
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,000
Next, Sanpei.

109
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:17,840
Yes.

110
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:20,720
Did you grill this fish?

111
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:22,640
Y-yes, that's right.

112
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:24,720
It's a bit too much vinegar.

113
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:25,460
Yes.

114
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:26,680
And the seasoning too.

115
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,960
What's the problem with it?

116
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:31,500
You're being bossy as usual

117
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:32,908
No,

118
00:08:32,958 --> 00:08:36,720
I always thought Lemon had
no food preferences, but...

119
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:38,320
You don't, do you?

120
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:49,120
As expected, for mixed miso,
white miso should be six to four.

121
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,560
He always eats everything
without leaving a bite.

122
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,860
Though he's annoying with
all his know-it-all lectures.

123
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:55,560
Well, that's just it.

124
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:59,980
A brochure from the elementary school?

125
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:03,060
I had it sent for, for Lemon's sake.

126
00:09:03,060 --> 00:09:05,780
Grandma, you really are jumping the gun.

127
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,800
Being early isn't a bad thing, is it?

128
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:13,700
When Lemon enters elementary school,
you'll get school lunch instead of a bento!

129
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,180
What's school lunch?

130
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,860
It's the meal they serve you at school.

131
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:20,240
They serve it at school?

132
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,440
Look, the menu's printed right here.

133
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,380
It looks so delicious.

134
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:30,360
What's wrong, Lemon?

135
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,340
Nothing, really.

136
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:40,580
That's the brochure I
was looking at earlier.

137
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:45,000
Apparently there's something
on that menu you don't like.

138
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:50,420
This school lunch is far more
luxurious than anything from our day!

139
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:54,860
The eras are just too different.

140
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:57,340
In Kankichi's day,
it was all powdered skim milk, right?

141
00:09:58,040 --> 00:09:58,760
Well, yeah.

142
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:04,080
But I don't think there's anything
on here you'd dislike, Lemon.

143
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:08,760
Lemon has eaten everything on
the menu except white bread.

144
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:13,100
What? Lemon, you've never had white bread?

145
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:13,840
Yeah.

146
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:20,360
Now that you mention it, white bread is practically never served at Gibōshike.
It's an unknown food.

147
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:24,240
Could you ask me in a roundabout way?

148
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,020
Fine.

149
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:27,440
Hey, Lemon.

150
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:28,900
What is it, Kankichi?

151
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:34,120
This may be a random question,
but do you dislike white bread?

152
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,580
That's exactly what I said.

153
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:38,520
N-no, that's not true.

154
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:42,080
Come on, don't lie.
Your eyes are darting away.

155
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:48,580
They're not! I like white bread.

156
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:52,200
Then look at me.
Come on, look over here and say it.

157
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:55,820
You're so persistent,
that's why Kankichi can't get any girls.

158
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:56,540
What?

159
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:56,740
What?

160
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,800
Matoi always says that.

161
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:00,060
What did you say?

162
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:00,760
Hey!

163
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:02,600
I said no!

164
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,180
I only said it once.

165
00:11:04,180 --> 00:11:06,180
Mind your own business.

166
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:07,920
Calm down, Kankichi.

167
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,440
Lemon's...

168
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:11,900
Damn it!

169
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,480
Getting brushed off by a preschooler?
What an idiot.

170
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:14,940
Honestly.

171
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:17,200
Hey!

172
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:18,900
Lemon!

173
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,320
Where are you?!

174
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:26,900
I'm not saying it's bad to dislike bread.

175
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:29,900
There's a rule about
elementary school lunches,

176
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,440
you have to eat everything
without leaving any.

177
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,660
You're not allowed to leave any?

178
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:35,860
Even if you dislike it?

179
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:36,880
That's right.

180
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:39,820
Really? Matoi, is that really true?

181
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,280
That's the rule, you know.

182
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,220
What happens if you leave some?

183
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:50,420
In that case,
you get kept behind in the classroom.

184
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:54,760
Left behind

185
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:59,460
you'll be sentenced to the
upside-down pasting punishment.

186
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:03,440
Hehehehehehe

187
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,000
Don't tell such stupid lies.

188
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,440
That's right, Kankichi.

189
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,900
N-no, I don't want the upside-down pasting!

190
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:13,100
Look, you've scared Lemon.

191
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:16,780
Hey, now Lemon won't want
to go to elementary school!

192
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:17,920
That's right, you idiot.

193
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,080
Ow

194
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,200
Lemon, don't worry.

195
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,480
You won't get the upside-down pasting.

196
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,260
Phew, thank goodness.

197
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:29,620
But what are you going to
do with the bread you left?

198
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:33,220
If you leave it at lunch, then after school,

199
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:38,240
you have to eat it alone
in an empty classroom.

200
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:42,340
As he's doing that,
he senses someone behind him.

201
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:45,120
He slowly turns around.

202
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:47,060
Whoa!

203
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,180
Idiot!

204
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,180
Enough already!

205
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,400
You're scaring Lemon again.

206
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:58,680
Does Lemon really hate bread?

207
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,920
We don't have any at home to test him with.

208
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:03,080
I'll go buy some at the bakery.

209
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:13,280
Hey, Lemon

210
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,560
It's already showing on your face,
it's so obvious.

211
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:18,640
Really, it is.

212
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,840
You really can't eat it at all?

213
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:24,620
When you eat it, it's like...

214
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:27,960
It's like being stuck in the desert
eating biscuits until you die.

215
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:31,800
With your throat so dry it's at its limit.
It's that kind of feeling.

216
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,720
You haven't even eaten it, so I can't tell.

217
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:37,960
Anyway, just take one bite and try it.

218
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:39,260
Yeah.

219
00:13:42,020 --> 00:13:45,020
Now, what is it that
Lemon-chan is going to eat?

220
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:50,040
It's white bread!

221
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:53,580
Well then, let's have him eat it.

222
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,340
The taste test!

223
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:12,320
It's hopeless.

224
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,920
I give up.

225
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:18,400
Looks like he really is hopeless.

226
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:22,620
Remember when you ate my
katsu sandwich back in the day?

227
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:24,680
The katsu sandwich was moist and tender,

228
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:26,820
and if you washed it down with milk,
it was somehow fine.

229
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:29,480
But the problem is eating it on its own.

230
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:32,030
That dry, dry, crumbly,

231
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:34,680
it lacks that hafu-hafu feeling,
and that's the problem.

232
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,300
It's borderline

233
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,140
But we have to fix it
before he starts school.

234
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:44,880
I'm getting kind of depressed
about him going to school.

235
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:48,400
Seeing how he is now, I'm starting to worry.

236
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:49,000
Yeah.

237
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:53,060
Don't worry,
that's just him being a picky eater.

238
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:56,180
I'll make sure he learns to eat it.

239
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:00,960
Here's your chu-toro,
sorry to keep you waiting!

240
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,820
Milk colored with saffron.

241
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:09,540
Okay, okay, shape it and roll it up.

242
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:22,940
Put in the princess... then this one. What are you making?
You're making a dish with white bread, so you're trying to get him to eat it somehow.

243
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:27,900
I think fooling Lemon's tongue
is an extremely difficult feat.

244
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:28,300
Mm.

245
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:29,860
Mm.

246
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:30,940
Mm.

247
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:31,100
Mm.

248
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:31,900
This feeling, just like this.

249
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:38,440
Itadakimasu.

250
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,560
It smells like bread!

251
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:48,700
W-what are you talking about?

252
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,720
There's no bread anywhere!

253
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,560
R-right, Lemon!

254
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:54,220
What about this?

255
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,360
Thick omelette.

256
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:59,020
This is an omelette no
matter how you look at it.

257
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,060
Look, the inside is bread!

258
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,340
Sauce, in four colors!

259
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,940
Impressive.

260
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,080
What about this?

261
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:09,360
Firm tofu, it's delicious!

262
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,000
It's sliced bread!

263
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,244
Wow, what a surprise,

264
00:16:14,294 --> 00:16:18,320
finding bread mixed in here of all places!

265
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,080
It still smells like bread.

266
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:21,680
Gulp.

267
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,000
What's in this miso soup?

268
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:25,520
It's fried tofu.

269
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:28,220
This is bread too, see?

270
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:31,140
That's right! Miso soup with
bread that looks like fried tofu!

271
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,460
Well then, how about sushi?

272
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,380
The bottom is all bread!

273
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,180
That's right,
the new menu item: Western-style sushi!

274
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:40,260
I said I don't like bread!

275
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:43,182
R-right, that's what you said.

276
00:16:43,232 --> 00:16:45,780
Sorry, sorry. Hurry up and eat your rice.

277
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,460
Honestly...

278
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:54,000
Tch, damn it...

279
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,940
I don't want rice made by rolling up bread!

280
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:00,180
As if I'd ever do that!

281
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:02,720
Aww, I lost.

282
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:08,140
Lemon is a tough opponent.

283
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,180
There's no way you can fool me.

284
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,860
Damn it! I'm not giving up!

285
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:21,920
Alright, here we go, Lemon!

286
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,100
Nice catch!

287
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:31,620
Kankichi, I'm tired. Let's rest a bit.

288
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:33,680
What, you're already tired?

289
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:36,620
At this rate,
you won't get into elementary school.

290
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:41,760
Elementary school PE is tough,
unlike kindergarten.

291
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,560
Is that so?

292
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:49,520
At this rate, the teacher will tell you
to go back to kindergarten and start over.

293
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,060
That's no good.

294
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,140
Keep going, Kankichi!

295
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,480
They're just kids after all.

296
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,760
If we make them exercise until
they're worn out and starving,

297
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:02,020
Here it comes!

298
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:03,360
Hey!

299
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:05,380
Yah!

300
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:07,320
Here it comes!

301
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:12,560
How about it, Lemon? Are you tired?

302
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,380
No, it's nothing much.

303
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:19,760
Exercising that much
really works up an appetite.

304
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,940
For a grown-up, you're being pathetic.

305
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:28,760
When you're hungry, it doesn't
matter if you're a grown-up or a kid.

306
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:32,820
I'm hungry.

307
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:35,800
Grandma, is dinner ready yet?

308
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:38,560
Kikio and Matoi are bringing it out now.

309
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,560
Sorry to keep you waiting.

310
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:48,160
Let's eat.

311
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:49,940
Here we go.

312
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:58,560
Sorry, Lemon, we just ran out of rice.

313
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,520
Make do with this tonight, okay?

314
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:03,660
You ran out of rice at a sushi shop?

315
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:09,880
Never mind that, come on.

316
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:14,960
You're hungry, right?
It's definitely delicious. Itadakimasu!

317
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:20,180
The bread doesn't get in the
way of the solid ham flavor,

318
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:23,860
creating a harmony. It's delicious.

319
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:28,600
These vegetable sandwiches and egg sandwiches are delicious!
Exquisite!

320
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:30,260
I could eat these all day!

321
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,880
How about it?
Everyone's getting hungry now, right?

322
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:43,040
Wow, this is really good! I'm so hungry,
I could fit in as much of this as I want!

323
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,820
Yeah, delicious, delicious.

324
00:19:53,940 --> 00:20:21,600


325
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:24,400
Lemon, I'm sorry. I really mean it.

326
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,560
What are you talking about, Kankichi?

327
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:31,300
Kankichi must have eaten all
the bread Lemon doesn't like.

328
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:35,180
It's fine.
I'll have Sanpei make something for him.

329
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,960
He's too tough!

330
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,760
Ow ow!

331
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:45,980
No, it's just that Kankichi is an idiot.

332
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:47,160
Yeah.

333
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:51,420
Damn it. Looks like the last
resort is our only option now.

334
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:56,680
Eat your mandarin.

335
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,460
Don't worry about the mandarins.

336
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,600
Aren't you going to eat your mandarin?

337
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:05,540
Looks like he doesn't
like spinach baby food.

338
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:07,780
He eats the others well, though.

339
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:10,800
But I'll make you some cocoa now, okay?

340
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:11,460
Mm-hmm.

341
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:16,620
If you don't eat your mandarins properly,
you won't grow up big.

342
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:38,220
Mandarins.

343
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,820
Big sis Lemon has no food dislikes!

344
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:43,560
You don't dislike mandarins either, do you?

345
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:52,900
Mm.

346
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,660
Good job, mandarin!

347
00:21:59,580 --> 00:22:00,120
Mm.

348
00:22:00,730 --> 00:22:01,000
Mm.

349
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:10,580
What on earth is going on?

350
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,140
Well...

351
00:22:15,980 --> 00:22:18,220
Who convinced Lemon?

352
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:20,162
Mom did,

353
00:22:20,212 --> 00:22:23,220
she must be a seriously skilled negotiator.

354
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:26,229
But bread first thing in the morning...

355
00:22:26,279 --> 00:22:28,540
I've lived 102 years and
this is the first time!

356
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:37,940
Big sister must not be picky about her food.

357
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:42,160
Let's eat!

358
00:22:42,460 --> 00:22:42,820
Yes!

359
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,160
But what about you guys?

360
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,320
Well done!

361
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,100
It's delicious! So delicious, isn't it!

362
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:59,240
Is there any bad kid around here?

363
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,880
Who won't eat their bread?!

364
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:07,220
I'll gobble up any kid who won't eat!

365
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:14,980
He's eating it properly,
so no problem, right!

366
00:23:16,180 --> 00:23:17,500
W-what's going on here?

367
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:23,240
Lemon can eat white bread now.

368
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:25,600
Yeah, it's actually pretty good, Kankichi.

369
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:26,540
I see.

370
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:27,720
Kankichi.

371
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:31,260
Stop startling people like that.

372
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:32,880
Well, I didn't really do anything.

373
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:38,340
Wait, because of you,
I've lost at least a year off my life!

374
00:23:38,340 --> 00:23:41,140
Come on, you've already lived 102 years,
so what's a year or two?

375
00:23:41,140 --> 00:23:43,960
Losing a year or two doesn't matter,
does it?

376
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,580
Shut up!

377
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,020
Hey!

378
00:23:48,180 --> 00:23:49,080
Help me!

379
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:49,780
Wait!

380
00:23:50,140 --> 00:23:51,760
Let go and you'll understand!

381
00:23:51,860 --> 00:23:52,540
I get it already!

382
00:23:52,740 --> 00:23:53,740
Stop it!

383
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:54,600
There!

384
00:23:54,780 --> 00:23:55,500
Stop it!

385
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:59,340
You're going to love
starting elementary school!

386
00:24:00,260 --> 00:24:01,240
Stop!

387
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:02,740
Come on, go!

388
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:22,540
Why does Lemon, a kindergartener,
love period dramas, I wonder?

389
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:28,680
Why is the Chief's little mustache
a bit too small, I wonder?

390
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:36,600
Why does Honda's personality change
when he rides his motorbike, I wonder?

391
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:38,120
Four husbands

392
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:42,260
Why does the man who sleeps all day
only wake up once every four years?

393
00:24:42,260 --> 00:24:43,400
Why is that?

394
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:52,560
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryo-san,

395
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:56,320
but he lends out tanks
and fighter jets easily.

396
00:24:57,420 --> 00:24:59,620
Why is that?

397
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:06,940
Reiko is incredibly rich,

398
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:12,500
but she works at the police box.
Why is that?

399
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:16,000
Why is that, why is that?

400
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:19,560
Why, why, why, why is that?

401
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:33,280
You want me to become an
elementary school teacher?

402
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,780
Alright, leave it to me!

403
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:38,580
I've always wanted to try being a
teacher like the ones on TV dramas.

404
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:40,640
What the hell are these brats?

405
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:42,760
Everyone, listen to what I say!

406
00:25:43,240 --> 00:25:45,880
Next time: Class 3-B, Teacher Kankichi!

407
00:25:46,500 --> 00:25:47,260
Nice to meet you.

408
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,840
That's Kameari!

409
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:54,960
Well, it's definitely Kameari.

410
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:59,200
Everyone, come on over to our town!

411
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:00,760
Thank you.

